# internal/chacha8rand (step 9.11, ADR-102): the block function is Go's pure-Go block_generic; the assembly versions are not used.

@note Go's `chacha8_stub.s` is a jump to `block_generic` for the architectures without assembly; the patch writes that call. The record of offsets for the Loong64 assembly (`offsetLOONG64HasLSX`) is dropped with its import of `internal/cpu`.

@asm chacha8_stub.s the assembly stub that jumps to block_generic; the patch below writes the call in Go

@file chacha8.go
@why gocpp has no assembly: block is block_generic, as chacha8_stub.s does for the other architectures.
@replace
func block(seed *[4]uint64, blocks *[32]uint64, counter uint32)
@with
func block(seed *[4]uint64, blocks *[32]uint64, counter uint32) {
	block_generic(seed, blocks, counter)
}
@end

@why The offsets are for the Loong64 assembly, and name internal/cpu fields that gocpp's stub does not have.
@replace
// Offsets into internal/cpu records for use in assembly.
const (
	offsetLOONG64HasLSX = unsafe.Offsetof(cpu.Loong64.HasLSX)
)

@with
@end

@why Imports of the dropped constant.
@replace
	"internal/byteorder"
	"internal/cpu"
	"unsafe"
)
@with
	"internal/byteorder"
)
@end
